Build Fetcher began as a copy of Irelia Companion 2.2.0
(https://github.com/DobreValentinFlorinDan/irelia-companion, commit 919a8e3), by the same author.
It reuses that project's engineering:
  - the Rust workspace layout, and the CI and release workflows;
  - the Tauri v2 shell, tray and in-game overlay;
  - the Riot API client and its GCRA rate limiter;
  - the League client (LCU) connector, the Live Client tracker, and the rune and item-set importer;
  - the zstd codec, the correctly rounded math (jsmath) and JSON number formatting;
  - the CUDA driver loader and its self-check;
  - the Data Dragon loader, the item catalog and the exclusivity groups;
  - the synthetic match-v5 test kit.
Irelia Companion's model, evaluation, scraper, storage format and data are not carried over.

